node_modules/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
reports/runs/
reports/runpod-gpu/runs/
*.log
!corpus/90-verdicts/**/*.log
.DS_Store

# Reference video: sources are catalogued in corpus/70-visual/refs/_provenance.json and
# re-fetchable, but the bytes are too large to vendor. Clips under 40MB may be committed.
corpus/70-visual/refs/video/*.mp4
corpus/70-visual/refs/video/*.mkv
corpus/70-visual/refs/video/*.webm

# Raw capture frames. W1-30-EVIDENCE.md §5: "Not committed: raw PNG sequences, orbit frame dumps,
# transient moving derivatives." A full Deck run is 288 stills and 2,400 motion frames at ~880 KB
# each — a quarter of a gigabyte that any agent's routine `git add -A` would otherwise sweep into
# the tree (HAZARDS §3). The manifests, the per-frame HASHES and the contact sheets are the
# committed artefacts and are deliberately NOT ignored.
reports/visual-truth/deck/*/frames/
reports/visual-truth/deck-motion/*/frames/

# land.mjs conflict rescues. When land.mjs resolves a conflict it preserves the losing side here,
# which is a genuine safety net and has already been checked once (2026-08-14) and found to hold
# only a correctly-superseded older file — nothing was lost.
#
# But 194 of its first 198 files were rescue copies of GENERATED files (docs/index.html,
# docs/progress.html, docs/status.json, orchestration/INDEX.md), 48 MB of churn that regenerates on
# the next publish. Those are ignored; rescues of real SOURCE files are deliberately NOT ignored, so
# that if the net ever catches something that matters, it shows up in `git status` and someone looks.
reports/land-rescue/**/docs/
reports/land-rescue/**/orchestration/INDEX.md
reports/land-rescue/**/*.error.json
docs/data/cost-ledger.error.json
